# The names of the settings the gateway reads from the environment. Names only, never values.
#
# BIOHACK_BACKEND_TOKEN — the credential the gateway presents to a GPU backend as `X-Backend-Token`.
# It must hold the value those backends were started with (`-e BACKEND_TOKEN=…`), and it is the only
# lock on that hop: a backend sits behind a router whose address every tailnet peer wears, so nothing
# below the application can tell the gateway from any other machine on the overlay. Unset, the model
# surface refuses every inference with `503` rather than letting a backend answer `401`, which would
# read like the participant's fault. It is set by hand in `~/.config/biohack-gateway/env` on the host,
# never here; the reasoning is in deploy/gpu-backends.md and deploy/README.md §1.5.
#
# systemd hands that file to the process through `EnvironmentFile=`. It exists even when it holds
# nothing, because a missing state file must fail the start rather than let the service run with
# defaults.
#
# The gateway's two *surface* settings — the directory of `<dataset>.db` files and the base URL images
# are addressed from — are `create_app` parameters whose defaults already hold the live values, so
# moving either is a code change rather than a variable, and neither appears here.
